// Title: HackTool - SafetyKatz Execution
// Sigma ID: b1876533-4ed5-4a83-90f3-b8645840a413
// Status: test | Level: critical
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-10-20 | Modified: 2023-02-04
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1003.001
// Description: Detects the execution of the hacktool SafetyKatz via PE information and default Image name
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://github.com/GhostPack/SafetyKatz
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_safetykatz.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\SafetyKatz.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "SafetyKatz.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoFileDescription =~ "SafetyKatz"
